 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Gosh is short way of saying goodness gracious how time flies. It' particularly British and dates back to the 1920s. Exactly. People used to write it with watercolor and then with a thick black pen. It gave everything a friendly, old-fashioned look. It' a nice way to practice without overthinking each stroke. Fill in the lines with little doodles as you go. Fill in the background first, then work on the main subject. Starting with the subject can make the background look too plain. Exactly. Now go and get a fresh sheet of paper and try it. You might surprise yourself.",
